<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴπερ</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ
			περ</span></b> , strengthd. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>if really, if indeed</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				3.25
			</span></i>, etc.; esp. <i>even if, even though</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.117
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				1.167
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ. καί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.35
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ. τε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					10.225
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ. γε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					198
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				312a
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ. γε δή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					182c
				</span></i>
			; with words between, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ. γάρ τε
				χόλον γε</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.81
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴπερ ἔσται γε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1249
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				275e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλῶς, εἴπερ ποτέ, ἔχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					4.20
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴπερ ἄρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					7.216b
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in 
				Att.
			 and Trag. to imply that the supposition agrees with the
			fact, <i>if as is the fact, since</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				6.14
			</span></i>, etc.; but with impf. it implies that it is
			contrary to the fact, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴπερ ἦν πέλας</span>
			<i>if</i> I had been (but I was not), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>El.</u>
				312
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				604
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ. ἐκτελεῖς ἅπερ λέγεις</span>
			<i>if only</i> you will keep your word, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ichn.</u>
				48
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> with an
			ellipse, <i>if you must</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				227
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλ᾽ εἴ.</span> but <i>if
			so</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prm.</u>
				150b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1101a12
			</span></i>; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
				</span></i>
			 VII.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
